The SCEPTRE bennu module now flags firmware that enables the brash shell (``firmware.extra.shell_enabled``) and records whether ``bennu-watcherd`` accepts the uploaded firmware (``firmware.extra.watcher_accepted``). When the shell is enabled, it checks TCP 1337 and adds a brash service and an alert event. The FTP account is recorded as a user, and internal tag initial values are stored with their type in the new ``Tag.extra`` field instead of in the tag description.
